{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1145930-confusion-about-format-and-merit-prerequisites","id":1145930,"title":"Confusion about format and merit prerequisites","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-01T18:16:34-07:00","id":1145930,"title":"Confusion about format and merit prerequisites","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> This is more of a rant than a question on my part, but please indulge my curiosity, why do some merits have Attribute/Skill \u2022\u2022\u2022+ ? I mean what is the difference between that, and saying &quot;Attribute/Skill at 4 dots&quot;???<br /> <br /> Actually, I am confused, if a merit says Relevant Stat at \u2022\u2022\u2022+ is 3 and higher, or 4?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-01-2017, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T18:38:26-07:00","id":1145936,"title":"","content":"It's shorthand for three-and-higher, yes. In almost all cases there's no difference between seeing a prerequisite of Strength \u2022\u2022\u2022 and of Strength \u2022\u2022\u2022+, likely a quirk between writers not caught in the editing. I'd guess the intent is to make more clear that these Merits can be taken at higher dot levels as well - contrast with the rare Merits that stipulate both a minimum and maximum, like second edition Werewolf's Blood Affinity and Bone Affinity Merits, which must be taken while their Harmony is between three and eight dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T22:25:20-07:00","id":1145982,"title":"","content":"Some Merits also internally scale, where your dots in it are limited by your dots in a prerequisite trait. I can't think of any 2e examples, but I know there are 1e Merits that had this sort of notation when you had to increase the base trait to continue to raise the Merit. I'd have to go back and looks to see if this was/is consistent, since it's a useful way to note this quirk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T23:32:01-07:00","id":1145987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1145930-confusion-about-format-and-merit-prerequisites?p=1145982#post1145982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Merits also internally scale, where your dots in it are limited by your dots in a prerequisite trait. I can't think of any 2e examples, but I know there are 1e Merits that had this sort of notation when you had to increase the base trait to continue to raise the Merit. I'd have to go back and looks to see if this was/is consistent, since it's a useful way to note this quirk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only one I can think off the bat is Favored Form in Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}